1
00:00:00,507 --> 00:00:01,842
[mellow music playing]

2
00:00:01,925 --> 00:00:03,510
[Hina sobbing loudly]

3
00:00:09,766 --> 00:00:13,311
[Ayame] <i>This is the first time
I'm seeing someone cry this hard.</i>

4
00:00:14,646 --> 00:00:17,649
<i>All 'cause I had to stick my nose
in her business.</i>

5
00:00:21,903 --> 00:00:24,406
But, apparently,
they have some spares back in the gym.

6
00:00:24,489 --> 00:00:25,574
Could you get one for me?

7
00:00:27,034 --> 00:00:30,078
<i>If I hadn't tried to get
the two of them alone together...</i>

8
00:00:31,496 --> 00:00:35,083
{\an8}<i>What are you supposed to say to someone
at a time like this?</i>

9
00:00:36,209 --> 00:00:40,130
<i>If I were her and someone said,
"There are better guys out there,"</i>

10
00:00:40,213 --> 00:00:42,549
<i>I'd go, "Yeah? Let's see them then."</i>

11
00:00:43,133 --> 00:00:46,053
<i>And if they said,
"This must be hard for you,"</i>

12
00:00:46,136 --> 00:00:49,473
<i>it'd probably make me think,
"How could you know what I'm feeling?"</i>

13
00:00:49,556 --> 00:00:51,600
[Hina continues sobbing]

14
00:00:52,851 --> 00:00:57,147
[Ayame] <i>And anyway, I don't even know
what it's like to have a broken heart.</i>

15
00:00:59,566 --> 00:01:01,026
<i>What should I do?</i>

16
00:01:03,862 --> 00:01:05,572
[rustling]

17
00:01:12,162 --> 00:01:13,955
Why're you lining up tissues?

18
00:01:15,332 --> 00:01:18,794
I thought the barbecue would be messy,
so I brought a bunch of them.

19
00:01:18,877 --> 00:01:20,128
I am the manager.

20
00:01:20,712 --> 00:01:22,422
{\an8}They're all yours if you want.

21
00:01:24,007 --> 00:01:25,342
Thank you, Ayame.

22
00:01:32,307 --> 00:01:34,601
[Ayame] Let it all out. Don't hold it in.

23
00:01:35,185 --> 00:01:36,228
[Hina] Okay.

24
00:01:37,979 --> 00:01:40,023
[Ayame] You really like him, don't you?

25
00:01:40,649 --> 00:01:41,608
[Hina] Yeah.

26
00:01:42,192 --> 00:01:43,401
[continues sobbing]

27
00:01:51,618 --> 00:01:55,664
[Ayame] <i>Does Inota have any idea
that she likes him this much?</i>

28
00:01:57,791 --> 00:02:00,293
<i>Looking back on all the guys
who've asked me out,</i>

29
00:02:00,961 --> 00:02:04,589
<i>I wonder if any of them ever liked me
as much as she likes him.</i>

30
00:02:09,803 --> 00:02:11,596
<i>Nope. I guess not.</i>

31
00:02:20,689 --> 00:02:22,816
{\an8}<i>I know this must be painful,</i>

32
00:02:24,317 --> 00:02:28,864
<i>but she really fell for someone,
and I envy her for that.</i>

33
00:02:32,868 --> 00:02:34,870
[opening theme song playing]

34
00:02:59,269 --> 00:03:02,647
BLUE BOX

35
00:04:01,998 --> 00:04:03,833
{\an8}[Coach] Now, the bus home leaves at 5 p.m.

36
00:04:03,917 --> 00:04:04,918
{\an8}EPISODE 25
EVEN SO

37
00:04:05,001 --> 00:04:08,546
And we'll run scrimmages till then.
So, pack your stuff now.

38
00:04:10,382 --> 00:04:11,841
That's a fun pattern.

39
00:04:11,925 --> 00:04:13,176
It's my younger sister's.

40
00:04:14,094 --> 00:04:14,928
[Taiki gasps]

41
00:04:15,011 --> 00:04:16,930
[inaudible]

42
00:04:20,767 --> 00:04:21,768
[Taiki] Hey.

43
00:04:22,477 --> 00:04:24,187
I'm gonna head to the gym.

44
00:04:24,813 --> 00:04:26,815
Practice isn't for half an hour.

45
00:04:26,898 --> 00:04:28,733
I wanna practice my serves.

46
00:04:28,817 --> 00:04:29,818
Sure, man.

47
00:04:31,278 --> 00:04:33,488
[serene music playing]

48
00:04:33,571 --> 00:04:34,656
[grunts]

49
00:04:42,789 --> 00:04:44,207
[shuttlecock thudding]

50
00:04:55,468 --> 00:04:57,095
[Taiki] <i>I did the right thing.</i>

51
00:04:57,178 --> 00:05:00,473
<i>It would've hurt her more
if I hadn't made things clear.</i>

52
00:05:03,727 --> 00:05:05,520
<i>I told you that I'm fine with it!</i>

53
00:05:07,022 --> 00:05:08,106
{\an8}[grunts softly]

54
00:05:17,032 --> 00:05:18,283
- [Haryu] In.
- [gasps]

55
00:05:18,825 --> 00:05:22,329
You're going at it like
we haven't been practicing for three days.

56
00:05:23,913 --> 00:05:26,583
I'd never win
if a few days of practice tired me out.

57
00:05:26,666 --> 00:05:28,752
[Haryu chuckles] I like what I'm hearing.

58
00:05:29,586 --> 00:05:30,754
So then...

59
00:05:31,838 --> 00:05:33,965
You wanna play a match against me?

60
00:05:37,844 --> 00:05:40,013
- Love all. Play.
- Here's to a good game.

61
00:05:45,101 --> 00:05:47,896
Hey, Kyo, do you mind
going to wake up Nishida?

62
00:05:47,979 --> 00:05:49,022
Yeah, sounds good.

63
00:05:52,609 --> 00:05:53,735
GLOOMY

64
00:05:53,818 --> 00:05:56,362
[Ayame] <i>I meddled
in other people's business.</i>

65
00:05:56,446 --> 00:05:59,407
<i>I had no idea
things would turn out this way.</i>

66
00:06:00,617 --> 00:06:02,035
What's the matter?

67
00:06:02,118 --> 00:06:03,203
[Ayame gasps]

68
00:06:04,245 --> 00:06:05,538
[grunts angrily]

69
00:06:05,622 --> 00:06:08,666
{\an8}How about it's none of your business,
Kyo Kasahara?

70
00:06:08,750 --> 00:06:11,628
{\an8}Just stay out of it,
you nosy, meddling four-eyes!

71
00:06:19,886 --> 00:06:21,513
Just a shot in the dark, but...

72
00:06:22,138 --> 00:06:23,973
is this about Taiki and Hina?

73
00:06:24,933 --> 00:06:26,392
{\an8}Um... Uh...

74
00:06:27,644 --> 00:06:29,479
{\an8}You know about that?

75
00:06:32,065 --> 00:06:34,067
I thought something was up with them.

76
00:06:34,818 --> 00:06:36,945
They've been acting weird since yesterday.

77
00:06:39,405 --> 00:06:42,158
That means Taiki gave her his answer.

78
00:06:42,909 --> 00:06:44,828
[shuttlecock thudding]

79
00:06:44,911 --> 00:06:46,329
[both grunting]

80
00:06:46,412 --> 00:06:48,081
[emotional music playing]

81
00:06:48,665 --> 00:06:49,707
Eight, four.

82
00:06:51,251 --> 00:06:54,087
[pants] Darn it.

83
00:06:54,671 --> 00:06:57,799
[girl 1] So it's the last time
we're going down this road, huh?

84
00:06:57,882 --> 00:07:00,093
[girl 2] Let's make
this last practice count.

85
00:07:07,183 --> 00:07:09,727
I just can't seem
to wrap my head around it.

86
00:07:11,855 --> 00:07:14,858
Like, this is the first that I'm hearing
Inota has feelings for somebody.

87
00:07:14,941 --> 00:07:15,859
What the heck?

88
00:07:15,942 --> 00:07:16,985
[Kyo] Uh...

89
00:07:18,236 --> 00:07:19,112
Anyway...

90
00:07:20,613 --> 00:07:23,366
{\an8}finding someone who'll fall
head over heels for you like Hina-bean,

91
00:07:24,242 --> 00:07:25,702
{\an8}<i>it doesn't happen every day.</i>

92
00:07:27,954 --> 00:07:30,832
{\an8}This would all make sense
if he had no interest in her,

93
00:07:30,915 --> 00:07:33,042
{\an8}but as friends, they get along so well.

94
00:07:33,626 --> 00:07:34,752
{\an8}I don't get it.

95
00:07:35,378 --> 00:07:37,922
{\an8}Well, I do. They're really good friends.

96
00:07:39,340 --> 00:07:42,177
Hina would be upset
if she heard me say this, but...

97
00:07:44,721 --> 00:07:48,308
I think that those two make more sense
if they're just close friends.

98
00:07:48,391 --> 00:07:49,392
[Ayame exclaims]

99
00:07:49,476 --> 00:07:51,186
[groans]

100
00:07:51,269 --> 00:07:53,146
Taiki prefers to pursue a crush.

101
00:07:53,229 --> 00:07:55,398
I don't think he's used to being pursued.

102
00:07:56,107 --> 00:07:58,526
I guess caring for someone as a friend

103
00:07:58,610 --> 00:08:00,737
and caring about them
as a romantic partner

104
00:08:00,820 --> 00:08:02,155
are two different things.

105
00:08:03,740 --> 00:08:04,657
[Ayame] Hmm.

106
00:08:05,200 --> 00:08:07,327
- It is what it is.
- [exclaims]

107
00:08:08,328 --> 00:08:09,913
You say that like it's no big deal.

108
00:08:10,622 --> 00:08:11,873
It's all I can say.

109
00:08:12,582 --> 00:08:14,959
You and I are on the sidelines,
not the field.

110
00:08:16,252 --> 00:08:17,670
<i>Taiki made his choice.</i>

111
00:08:17,754 --> 00:08:19,172
[both grunting]

112
00:08:19,756 --> 00:08:22,008
[Taiki] <i>A straight shot.
No, a cross-court.</i>

113
00:08:28,806 --> 00:08:30,058
Thirteen, six.

114
00:08:31,059 --> 00:08:32,018
[exhales heavily]

115
00:08:32,101 --> 00:08:34,187
{\an8}[Taiki] <i>He's not letting me score at all.</i>

116
00:08:35,104 --> 00:08:37,732
<i>I've been wondering
why he wouldn't play me lately.</i>

117
00:08:41,110 --> 00:08:42,695
<i>He went and got even better.</i>

118
00:08:42,779 --> 00:08:45,406
<i>I want to catch up to him.
I don't want to lose.</i>

119
00:08:45,490 --> 00:08:49,452
<i>If Haryu can become a stronger player,
then I can get better too.</i>

120
00:08:50,537 --> 00:08:52,622
<i>Better! Way better!</i>

121
00:08:53,456 --> 00:08:54,541
[grunts]

122
00:08:55,500 --> 00:08:56,459
[Haryu] Out!

123
00:08:56,543 --> 00:08:58,044
Game, set, match.

124
00:08:58,670 --> 00:09:00,421
Thanks for the practice.

125
00:09:00,505 --> 00:09:01,464
Wait, what?

126
00:09:02,298 --> 00:09:03,424
One more game.

127
00:09:03,508 --> 00:09:05,426
Yeah, I figured you would say that.

128
00:09:05,510 --> 00:09:06,719
Nah, we're done here.

129
00:09:07,303 --> 00:09:10,682
And it's the last day
of training camp, after all. I'm tired.

130
00:09:12,684 --> 00:09:14,018
{\an8}One game's not fair.

131
00:09:17,438 --> 00:09:18,314
[sighs]

132
00:09:20,441 --> 00:09:22,527
Listen, being honest...

133
00:09:24,112 --> 00:09:27,240
I was actually kinda nervous
to play against you.

134
00:09:28,074 --> 00:09:29,200
What?

135
00:09:30,034 --> 00:09:31,995
<i>This guy? Afraid?</i>

136
00:09:32,078 --> 00:09:33,663
Embarrassing, right?

137
00:09:35,915 --> 00:09:38,751
<i>After everything,
I was never able to beat Hyodo.</i>

138
00:09:38,835 --> 00:09:41,879
<i>That jerk had to go and quit
before I was done with him.</i>

139
00:09:42,797 --> 00:09:46,426
<i>And then, I couldn't beat
that first-year Yusa in a practice match.</i>

140
00:09:46,968 --> 00:09:49,804
I thought if I lost to you
on top of all of that,

141
00:09:50,388 --> 00:09:52,682
I wouldn't have a drop of confidence left.

142
00:09:52,765 --> 00:09:54,892
[mellow music playing]

143
00:09:55,476 --> 00:09:57,604
Well, in the end, I always win.

144
00:09:57,687 --> 00:09:58,855
[sighs heavily]

145
00:09:59,897 --> 00:10:01,149
[sighs]

146
00:10:01,232 --> 00:10:02,900
I'm glad we played each other.

147
00:10:02,984 --> 00:10:06,195
Besides, if I had kept putting it off,
that'd be so pathetic.

148
00:10:06,988 --> 00:10:11,618
Being afraid of losing,
having my stupid pride torn to pieces...

149
00:10:12,910 --> 00:10:16,456
<i>I have to make my own peace with it,
reflect on it,</i>

150
00:10:17,081 --> 00:10:18,916
<i>and use it to keep moving forward.</i>

151
00:10:20,043 --> 00:10:23,129
That's what makes a strong player,
to me, anyway.

152
00:10:33,598 --> 00:10:35,391
Everybody is so strong.

153
00:10:36,142 --> 00:10:37,560
What do you mean?

154
00:10:37,644 --> 00:10:39,687
- You're strong too.
- [gasps]

155
00:10:48,988 --> 00:10:49,989
[music fades]

156
00:10:52,075 --> 00:10:53,493
{\an8}EIMEI PRIVATE HIGH SCHOOL

157
00:11:05,588 --> 00:11:07,256
- Chinatsu.
- [exclaims]

158
00:11:07,882 --> 00:11:10,426
Taiki. Hey, welcome home.

159
00:11:10,510 --> 00:11:12,345
You too, Chinatsu, welcome home.

160
00:11:12,845 --> 00:11:13,888
Here I am.

161
00:11:14,472 --> 00:11:15,515
Here we are.

162
00:11:16,099 --> 00:11:17,266
{\an8}This feels weird.

163
00:11:17,350 --> 00:11:18,393
[gasps]

164
00:11:22,313 --> 00:11:24,273
- Chinatsu.
- Hmm?

165
00:11:24,857 --> 00:11:28,069
Could the two of us
go somewhere on our next day off?

166
00:11:40,456 --> 00:11:42,291
- Where?
- I, uh...

167
00:11:42,875 --> 00:11:44,502
<i>Where should we go?</i>

168
00:11:44,585 --> 00:11:46,754
<i>An amusement park is too obvious, right?</i>

169
00:11:46,838 --> 00:11:49,048
<i>And we already went to the aquarium.</i>

170
00:11:49,132 --> 00:11:50,299
{\an8}<i>What else is there?</i>

171
00:11:50,383 --> 00:11:53,302
{\an8}<i>Uh... Shopping for something
I've been wanting to get?</i>

172
00:11:53,886 --> 00:11:56,806
A tracksuit!
I've been wanting to buy a new one!

173
00:11:56,889 --> 00:11:59,809
The one I have is worn out after camp,
so I should replace it!

174
00:12:00,435 --> 00:12:02,228
- [Chinatsu grunts softly]
- What do you say?

175
00:12:02,895 --> 00:12:07,066
<i>Why did I say "tracksuit"?
That's not exactly sexy.</i>

176
00:12:07,650 --> 00:12:09,861
- Sure.
- Are you serious?

177
00:12:09,944 --> 00:12:13,573
But in return, there's a cafe
that I've been wanting to stop by.

178
00:12:13,656 --> 00:12:14,824
Could we go check it out?

179
00:12:15,450 --> 00:12:17,577
Uh... yeah, for sure.

180
00:12:18,202 --> 00:12:19,162
Sounds great.

181
00:12:21,122 --> 00:12:22,790
How about next Saturday?

182
00:12:22,874 --> 00:12:25,585
- You have practice in the morning, right?
- Yes.

183
00:12:26,210 --> 00:12:28,087
Okay, next Saturday it is.

184
00:12:33,176 --> 00:12:34,343
[thudding]

185
00:12:38,681 --> 00:12:39,724
<i>It's a date!</i>

186
00:12:41,184 --> 00:12:43,311
<i>We're just going to buy a tracksuit,</i>

187
00:12:43,394 --> 00:12:46,606
<i>but it'll be our first outing
since the aquarium, the beach?</i>

188
00:12:46,689 --> 00:12:50,693
<i>And it seemed like
Chinatsu was pretty excited about it too.</i>

189
00:12:50,776 --> 00:12:54,614
<i>You have to get your act together!
Show her what a man you are, Taiki!</i>

190
00:12:57,325 --> 00:13:00,620
<i>This is my chance to tell her how I feel.</i>

191
00:13:21,724 --> 00:13:24,143
Hi, Hina-bean! Let's go have some fun.

192
00:13:24,227 --> 00:13:25,394
What?

193
00:13:26,062 --> 00:13:28,898
- Like, right now?
- We've been cooped up the last three days.

194
00:13:28,981 --> 00:13:31,108
So we gotta go out and make up for it.

195
00:13:31,192 --> 00:13:32,860
[Hina] What about all our stuff?

196
00:13:32,944 --> 00:13:34,904
[Ayame] That's what
coin lockers are for, girl!

197
00:13:34,987 --> 00:13:36,822
<i>When you're going through something,</i>

198
00:13:36,906 --> 00:13:39,825
<i>the best thing you can do
is keep yourself from thinking about it.</i>

199
00:13:39,909 --> 00:13:41,035
[camera shutter clicks]

200
00:13:41,118 --> 00:13:42,787
[Hina] That doesn't really look like me.

201
00:13:42,870 --> 00:13:44,914
[Ayame] Come on, that's what makes it fun!

202
00:13:44,997 --> 00:13:47,500
Oh, that shade looks stunning on you.

203
00:13:48,000 --> 00:13:50,586
[Hina] I've never actually
worn lipstick before.

204
00:13:50,670 --> 00:13:52,171
Then we'll buy one sometime.

205
00:13:52,255 --> 00:13:54,006
Yeah. Let's.

206
00:13:55,258 --> 00:13:58,010
Hockey! Let's do air hockey next!

207
00:13:58,094 --> 00:13:59,679
I've never played though.

208
00:13:59,762 --> 00:14:02,848
[Ayame] What?
This is 20% of the joy in life.

209
00:14:02,932 --> 00:14:04,183
[Hina] 20%?

210
00:14:04,267 --> 00:14:07,937
[Ayame] And FYI,
the seasonal Häagen-Dazs flavors are 50%.

211
00:14:08,020 --> 00:14:10,565
[Hina] I've somehow missed
70% of life's joy.

212
00:14:10,648 --> 00:14:13,192
[Ayame] Let's reclaim that 20%.
Here we go!

213
00:14:13,276 --> 00:14:15,194
- [Hina exclaims]
- [game chiming]

214
00:14:15,278 --> 00:14:17,029
[exclaims] That's how it's done.

215
00:14:17,113 --> 00:14:19,198
[Hina] You're not gonna
let me enjoy this, are you?

216
00:14:20,783 --> 00:14:21,701
Ha!

217
00:14:22,326 --> 00:14:24,328
[chuckles] Take that!

218
00:14:24,412 --> 00:14:25,705
[game chiming]

219
00:14:25,788 --> 00:14:28,749
- Winner!
- [Hina grunting angrily]

220
00:14:29,542 --> 00:14:31,168
{\an8}TAIKO MAESTRO
BEAT IT

221
00:14:31,252 --> 00:14:32,461
{\an8}[Ayame] You've done this one?

222
00:14:32,545 --> 00:14:34,964
- [Hina] Punch it, punch it!
- [Ayame whimpers]

223
00:14:36,299 --> 00:14:37,717
[both exclaiming]

224
00:14:37,800 --> 00:14:39,719
[Hina groans]

225
00:14:40,303 --> 00:14:43,306
[Ayame] <i>What a relief.
Looks like she's cheered up a bit.</i>

226
00:14:43,806 --> 00:14:46,267
<i>I'm gonna make sure
she has a blast tonight.</i>

227
00:14:47,018 --> 00:14:48,686
- [boy] Ayame? Is that you?
- Uh?

228
00:14:48,769 --> 00:14:51,272
Oh, what, you know this chick?
She's pretty hot.

229
00:14:51,355 --> 00:14:52,732
My ex-girlfriend.

230
00:14:53,316 --> 00:14:54,483
[sighs]

231
00:14:55,234 --> 00:14:56,736
Wait, are you an idiot, man?

232
00:14:56,819 --> 00:14:58,321
Why'd you end things with her?

233
00:14:58,404 --> 00:14:59,405
Well...

234
00:14:59,488 --> 00:15:00,489
Let me tell you,

235
00:15:00,573 --> 00:15:03,242
she kind of has
this "princess" thing going on.

236
00:15:03,910 --> 00:15:06,996
She got on me for everything.
How I talk to cashiers...

237
00:15:07,079 --> 00:15:09,999
She always told me
I don't enunciate enough when I order.

238
00:15:10,833 --> 00:15:13,628
What I was looking for
was something more casual.

239
00:15:15,379 --> 00:15:19,091
[Ayame] <i>He may have been a little awkward,
but I thought he was a nice guy.</i>

240
00:15:19,175 --> 00:15:22,011
[boy] <i>She wasn't the girl
I thought she was gonna be, you know?</i>

241
00:15:22,094 --> 00:15:24,305
[Ayame] <i>I wasn't a good judge
of character, I guess.</i>

242
00:15:24,847 --> 00:15:26,098
Why don't we go?

243
00:15:26,724 --> 00:15:29,268
[boy] None of your relationships last,
huh, not just with me?

244
00:15:30,353 --> 00:15:33,314
Your older sister
has a handsome boyfriend, right?

245
00:15:33,397 --> 00:15:36,275
You should follow her example
and be more considerate of--

246
00:15:36,359 --> 00:15:38,486
- Listen!
- Think you're right all you want.

247
00:15:38,569 --> 00:15:40,529
It's what keeps you going, isn't it?

248
00:15:40,613 --> 00:15:41,697
Huh?

249
00:15:41,781 --> 00:15:45,701
If you really believe what you're saying,
then you're not a good judge of character.

250
00:15:46,619 --> 00:15:49,538
If you convince yourself
that you're the rational one

251
00:15:49,622 --> 00:15:52,541
and the one who dumped you
is crazy and made the wrong choice,

252
00:15:53,417 --> 00:15:56,796
then all the time you spent
loving the other person

253
00:15:57,755 --> 00:16:00,007
{\an8}doesn't have to feel like it was a waste.

254
00:16:00,091 --> 00:16:01,300
{\an8}[sobs]

255
00:16:01,384 --> 00:16:02,385
[gasps]

256
00:16:02,885 --> 00:16:04,887
[grunts angrily] And, dude,

257
00:16:04,971 --> 00:16:07,890
I'll leak your secret social media profile
if you come at me again!

258
00:16:07,974 --> 00:16:08,808
[boy] No, not that!

259
00:16:09,892 --> 00:16:12,186
- I'm sorry.
- Not at all.

260
00:16:12,269 --> 00:16:14,271
You did nothing wrong, Hina-bean.

261
00:16:15,231 --> 00:16:16,649
Not a single thing.

262
00:16:18,651 --> 00:16:21,570
{\an8}EIMEI PRIVATE HIGH SCHOOL

263
00:16:28,285 --> 00:16:29,245
[grunts]

264
00:16:29,829 --> 00:16:30,788
[sighs]

265
00:16:39,338 --> 00:16:41,674
- [grunts]
- Whoopsies, my bad!

266
00:16:42,341 --> 00:16:44,218
Hey, was that on purpose?

267
00:16:44,301 --> 00:16:47,138
Take these! I need help
getting them into the storage room.

268
00:16:47,638 --> 00:16:48,764
Yes, ma'am.

269
00:16:49,974 --> 00:16:53,602
[Taiki] Ever since the training camp,
it seems like you've been mad at me.

270
00:16:53,686 --> 00:16:55,271
If I did something wrong, then...

271
00:16:56,188 --> 00:16:57,773
It was nothing in particular.

272
00:16:57,857 --> 00:17:00,026
[Taiki] <i>It was something, all right.</i>

273
00:17:00,818 --> 00:17:01,777
[Ayame] It's just...

274
00:17:04,864 --> 00:17:06,866
Hina-bean was crying, you know?

275
00:17:09,827 --> 00:17:10,786
I know.

276
00:17:10,870 --> 00:17:12,538
What do you mean you know?!

277
00:17:13,122 --> 00:17:15,041
<i>Whatever pain you think she's feeling,</i>

278
00:17:15,124 --> 00:17:17,626
<i>it's probably 100 times worse than that.</i>

279
00:17:18,127 --> 00:17:20,629
{\an8}And you act like
it doesn't bother you-- [gasps]

280
00:17:24,884 --> 00:17:25,885
I get it,

281
00:17:25,968 --> 00:17:31,057
but given how things are right now,
I can't just go up and talk to her.

282
00:17:31,932 --> 00:17:33,976
I've told her where I stand on things.

283
00:17:34,602 --> 00:17:38,564
All I can do now
is wait for her to decide what to do next.

284
00:17:39,398 --> 00:17:43,069
It would be selfish of me to ask her
to go back to being my friend.

285
00:17:45,071 --> 00:17:48,365
[Ayame] <i>So Inota does care for her
in his own way.</i>

286
00:17:49,492 --> 00:17:51,619
<i>Just not romantically.</i>

287
00:17:53,829 --> 00:17:54,955
I don't get it.

288
00:17:55,039 --> 00:17:58,292
Why you would turn down
someone like Hina-bean in the first place?

289
00:17:59,668 --> 00:18:03,839
This person you have feelings for,
are they really that great?

290
00:18:04,423 --> 00:18:05,633
[gasps]

291
00:18:07,760 --> 00:18:08,844
Hey!

292
00:18:08,928 --> 00:18:10,554
Practice is about to start.

293
00:18:10,638 --> 00:18:11,514
Got it!

294
00:18:13,432 --> 00:18:15,351
[Taiki] <i>What kind of question is that?</i>

295
00:18:15,976 --> 00:18:20,022
<i>If my answer was yes, it would
make it sound like Hina isn't great.</i>

296
00:18:29,532 --> 00:18:30,366
[Kyo grunts]

297
00:18:30,449 --> 00:18:31,617
What?

298
00:18:31,700 --> 00:18:32,868
It's nothing.

299
00:18:34,578 --> 00:18:35,579
If I had to guess,

300
00:18:35,663 --> 00:18:38,374
you think I'm meddling
in other people's business, huh?

301
00:18:38,999 --> 00:18:40,876
That face says I'm totally right.

302
00:18:42,795 --> 00:18:44,630
I may be an outsider in all of this.

303
00:18:45,214 --> 00:18:49,635
But seeing Hina that upset and crying,
it made me want to know why.

304
00:18:50,344 --> 00:18:52,888
And I always tell it like it is!
Unapologetically.

305
00:18:52,972 --> 00:18:55,641
Because that's who I am! Deal with it!

306
00:18:56,225 --> 00:19:00,646
I don't care what anybody thinks about me.
However they see me, that's on them.

307
00:19:01,355 --> 00:19:02,439
[sighs]

308
00:19:03,023 --> 00:19:04,441
But, you know,

309
00:19:04,525 --> 00:19:08,404
I do think you've been a life raft,
keeping Hina afloat through some of this.

310
00:19:09,155 --> 00:19:11,448
So having someone like you isn't all bad.

311
00:19:11,991 --> 00:19:13,617
[exclaims softly]

312
00:19:16,203 --> 00:19:18,664
[Ayame] You're a bit condescending,
you know that?

313
00:19:18,747 --> 00:19:20,916
- First time I've heard that.
- Huh?

314
00:19:23,794 --> 00:19:24,837
Uh, what's that?

315
00:19:25,504 --> 00:19:28,340
[Hina] Lil' Bunny Ears.
We made it for the Cultural Festival.

316
00:19:29,466 --> 00:19:34,096
It's a trick I use sometimes.
Blacking out my vision helps me to focus.

317
00:19:34,180 --> 00:19:36,015
All righty then, Hina.

318
00:19:36,098 --> 00:19:37,892
We'll just postpone your turn.

319
00:19:42,938 --> 00:19:45,524
[groans, sniffles]

320
00:19:48,861 --> 00:19:51,405
<i>I wish I could just blow up the gym.</i>

321
00:19:52,781 --> 00:19:55,868
<i>I didn't want to skip practice
because I got rejected.</i>

322
00:19:57,036 --> 00:20:00,873
<i>But being in the same space
with Taiki and Chinatsu,</i>

323
00:20:01,707 --> 00:20:03,542
<i>I feel like I can't breathe.</i>

324
00:20:03,626 --> 00:20:04,877
[indistinct chatter]

325
00:20:10,466 --> 00:20:12,801
[Taiki] Kyo! Have you seen
my phone anywhere?

326
00:20:12,885 --> 00:20:14,887
[Kyo] You left it on that chair earlier.

327
00:20:15,554 --> 00:20:17,640
[Taiki] Oh, yeah, there it is. Thanks!

328
00:20:18,140 --> 00:20:19,767
[boy] Hey, Taiki! Let's get some food.

329
00:20:19,850 --> 00:20:20,893
[Taiki] Sorry, I'm busy!

330
00:20:21,852 --> 00:20:23,062
See you later! Bye!

331
00:20:24,271 --> 00:20:27,149
Whoa, what's up with Taiki?
Why was he in such a hurry?

332
00:20:27,233 --> 00:20:28,984
Maybe he's got a date.

333
00:20:29,068 --> 00:20:30,152
[Nishida] What?!

334
00:20:30,236 --> 00:20:33,322
- Chill out, man, I'm just joking around.
- [Nishida] You better be!

335
00:20:33,405 --> 00:20:35,783
He, of all people,
would never betray me like that!

336
00:20:35,866 --> 00:20:37,159
[Haryu] Hmm?

337
00:20:37,243 --> 00:20:38,911
Wait. He does?

338
00:20:38,994 --> 00:20:42,414
I mean, it's not like he told me
that it's actually happening, but...

339
00:20:42,498 --> 00:20:44,333
Do you think he's going out with...

340
00:20:44,416 --> 00:20:45,459
{\an8}Probably.

341
00:20:45,542 --> 00:20:47,253
{\an8}[laughs]

342
00:20:47,753 --> 00:20:50,923
I've been wondering
how long he was gonna stew on that.

343
00:20:52,424 --> 00:20:55,135
<i>It's more like him
to just leap and let the net appear.</i>

344
00:20:56,262 --> 00:20:57,680
[Taiki panting]

345
00:20:57,763 --> 00:20:59,682
[pleasant music playing]

346
00:21:02,017 --> 00:21:04,186
<i>In front of the planters,
in front of the planters.</i>

347
00:21:04,270 --> 00:21:05,187
[gasps]

348
00:21:08,315 --> 00:21:10,192
[boy] You see that girl back there?
She's cute.

349
00:21:16,615 --> 00:21:17,908
What are you looking at?

350
00:21:18,534 --> 00:21:20,369
Well, uh...

351
00:21:20,452 --> 00:21:23,580
I was thinking that
the clouds are moving fast today.

352
00:21:50,983 --> 00:21:51,984
[music fades]

353
00:21:52,609 --> 00:21:54,611
[closing theme song playing]
